SUMMARY:HarpSound Live presents Harmony Winds: Legacy
LOCATION:1213 N. Central Avenue Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:HarpSound Live presents Harmony Winds: Legacy\, which examines
  five generations of gospel music through the history and performances of 
 a Tampa family whose musical tradition has continued across decades. The p
 rogram traces the familys development from the Singing Sisters\, an early 
 a cappella group founded by Ethel Pittman with her sister Bertha and frien
 d Annie Lou\, through church choirs and the Maranatha Singers\, establishe
 d as a performing group by 1979. Later generations expanded the familys mu
 sical practice beyond vocal performance\, cultivating instrumentalists and
  developing new ensembles. Today\, younger members continue that work thro
 ugh groups including the Tampa Boyz\, Simply Redeemed and Voices of Harmon
 y. Through live music and family history\, the concert considers how gospe
 l traditions are taught\, adapted and sustained across generations. Its fo
 cus on the relationships among family\, faith and performance also offers 
 a perspective on the role of gospel music in Tampas cultural history. Pres
 ented by Unlimited Gospel Expressions\, the event brings performers from d
 ifferent generations together at Tampas Black History Museum on Thursday\,
  Nov. 19\, 2026. Audiences will hear musical styles associated with succes
 sive periods of the familys history and consider how performance can prese
 rve personal memories\, document community experience and transmit cultura
 l knowledge to younger musicians. \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa.gov/nod
 e/197711
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/197711
END:VEVENT
