SUMMARY:Family Day: Directors Cut
LOCATION:801 Water Street Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Step behind the scenes of filmmaking at the Tampa Bay History 
 Centers Family Day: Directors Cut! Families are invited to explore the cre
 ative techniques that help bring stories to life on screen through a serie
 s of hands-on activities. Discover the art of Foley and experiment with cr
 eating sound effects using everyday household objects. Design costumes for
  paper doll characters and explore how filmmakers use lighting\, color\, s
 hadows\, and camera angles to shape the mood and atmosphere of a scene. Th
 is interactive family program offers visitors an opportunity to explore th
 e many creative roles involved in filmmaking while discovering how thought
 ful design\, sound\, and visual choices can transform a story. Join us in 
 the Wayne Thomas Gallery between 10 a.m. and 2 p.m. for this experience. E
 ntry to attend is through regular admission. \n\nPermalink: https://www.ta
 mpa.gov/node/197696
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/197696
