SUMMARY:Downtown Tampa Walking Tour
LOCATION:400 N. Franklin St.\, Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Explore downtown Tampa with T.J. Chaltry\, a History Center-tr
 ained guide and longtime Tampa resident whose passion for local history be
 gan with a visit to the Tampa Bay History Center. That experience inspired
  years of independent research into the people\, places and events that sh
 aped the city. For more than five years\, T.J. has shared that knowledge w
 ith walking tour guests\, transforming familiar streets and buildings into
  compelling connections to Tampas past. During this 90-minute tour\, T.J. 
 leads guests past landmarks including Old City Hall\, Sacred Heart Catholi
 c Church\, the Floridan Palace Hotel and The Hub\, Tampas oldest bar. Alon
 g the route\, guests will explore the architecture\, industries\, politica
 l conflicts and communities that contributed to downtown Tampas developmen
 t. The tour begins at Lykes Gaslight Park\, 400 N. Franklin St.\, Tampa\, 
 FL 33602. Participants will walk approximately one mile along public sidew
 alks and brick streets. Comfortable shoes and weather-appropriate clothing
  are recommended. Guests may also want to bring bottled water. Walking tou
 r tickets are 25 per person and must be purchased online in advance. Tours
  are limited to 25 participants\, so early registration is encouraged. Tou
 rs take place rain or shine\, and all ticket sales are final. If your plan
 s change and you are unable to attend\, please let us know so we can make 
 your spot available to others. History Center members save 20 on walking t
 ours and should log in before purchasing to apply the discount. \n\nPermal
 ink: https://www.tampa.gov/node/197701
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/197701
END:VEVENT
